# Skill: fresh-review

## When To Use

Use this rule when the user asks for `fresh-review` behavior, when an independent external
view would reduce risk, or when evidence-based review/triangulation is explicitly useful.

## When Not To Use

Do not use this for trivial checks, when a local deterministic command is faster, or
when the prompt would expose secrets, credentials, private auth files, shell history,
or session transcripts.

## Command Or Workflow

```bash
~/.agent-federation/bin/fresh-review --agent auto --cwd "$PWD" "<prompt>"
```

## Output Handling

Treat other-agent output as advisory. Extract claims, evidence, files inspected,
commands run, assumptions, confidence, and falsification paths. Verify before editing
files or presenting a conclusion.

## Safety Constraints

Default to read-only. Do not apply child-agent changes automatically. Do not decide by
majority vote. Keep artifacts local under `~/.agent-federation/logs`.
